{title: 279 - Only Trust Him}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Come, every soul by sin oppressed, There's [Em/B]mercy [Bm]with the Lord,
[G/D]And He [D]will [G/D]surely [Bm]give you rest, By trusting [C]in His word.
[G]Only trust Him, only trust Him, Only [Am/C]trust [Em/B]Him now;
[Bm]He will save [D7/C]you, He [Em/B]will [C]save you, He [G]will [Bm]save [Em/B]you [G/D]now.

Refrain:
[Bm]Only [D]trust [Bm]Him, only [D7/C]trust Him,
[Em/B]Only [C]trust Him now;
[G]He will save you, He will save you,
[D7/C]He will save [Em/B]you now.

Verse 2:
[G]For Jesus shed his [Am/C]precious [Bm]blood
[G/D]Rich [D]blessings [Bm/D]to bestow;
[G]Plunge now into the crimson [Em/B]flood
[Bm]That [D7/C]washes [C/G]white [G]as [Em/B]snow.

Verse 3:
[G]Yes, Jesus is the [Am/C]truth, [Bm]the way,
[G/D]That [D]leads [Bm]you into [C]rest;
[G]Believe in Him without [Am/C]delay,
[Bm]And [D7/C]you [Em/B]are [C/G]fully [Em/B]blest.

Verse 4:
[G]Come, then, and join this [Am/C]holy [Bm]band,
[G/D]And [D]on [Bm]to glory [C]go,
[G]To dwell in that celestial [Em/B]land,
[Bm]Where [D7/C]joys [Em/B]immortal flow.
